<title>USA: U.S. NAPM index 54.0 in Dec versus 52.7 in Nov.</title>
<headline>U.S. NAPM index 54.0 in Dec versus 52.7 in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) said on Thursday its index of maufacturing activity rose to 54.0 in December from 52.7 in November. A listing of the main NAPM components follows:</p>
<p>		   Dec  Nov   Oct   Sept  Aug   July  June  May</p>
<p>PMI	     54.0  52.7  50.2  51.7  52.6  50.2  54.3  49.3</p>
<p>Production    58.6  58.6  56.6  54.1  57.0  52.4  55.4  52.7</p>
<p>New Orders    58.3  55.4  51.6  56.3  55.6  54.0  61.3  52.4</p>
<p>Supplier Del  51.6  51.5  50.7  49.7  52.5  50.9  53.2  50.0</p>
<p>Inventories   45.8  41.8  38.9  44.8  41.6  41.2  42.3  38.3</p>
<p>Employment    47.7  47.5  45.5  46.9  48.2  45.5  49.4  45.5</p>
<p>Prices	  51.5  45.9  47.1  51.2  47.4  44.5  49.0  50.8</p>
<p>Export Orders 55.8  55.8  56.1  56.8  57.2  53.8  53.9  56.9</p>
<p>Imports	 51.4  52.5  53.8  51.8  50.6  53.7  48.6  49.8</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
